o"><country>JP</country><doc-number>51040153</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-57172555-A" status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>57172555</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-61283659-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>61283659</doc-number><kind>A</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1195400A1</text> <sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </nplcit> </non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>DAIKIN IND LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HASEGAWA MASANORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NOGUCHI TSUYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DAIKIN INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HASEGAWA, MASANORI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOGUCHI, TSUYOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HASEGAWA MASANORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NOGUCHI TSUYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HASEGAWA, MASANORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOGUCHI, TSUYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A carbon black filler for use in crosslinkable elastomer compositions which has a content of impurity metals of 300 ppm or lower and a pH of 5.0 to 11.0. It is obtained by extracting a raw carbon black filler with an acid to reduce the content of impurity metals therein and then treating the filler with an alkali to neutralize the acid remaining therein. Even when incorporated into an elastomer composition, the carbon black filler does not inhibit the crosslinking. It provides a molded elastomer especially suitable for use as an extremely clean sealing material for semiconductor manufacturing apparatuses.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>On décrit une matière de charge de noir de carbone utilisable dans des compositions élastomères réticulables et présentant une teneur en métaux impurs d'au plus 300 mg/l et un pH compris entre 5,0 et 11,0. Le procédé est réalisé par extraction d'une matière de charge de noir de carbone brute avec de l'acide afin d'en réduire la teneur en métaux impurs, puis par traitement de la matière de charge avec un alcali pour neutraliser l'acide résiduel. Même incorporée dans une composition élastomère, la matière de charge de noir de carbone ne fait pas obstacle à la réticulation. Elle donne un élastomère moulé particulièrement utile en tant que matière d'étanchéité extrêmement propre pour des appareils de production.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>